# CLAUDE.md — app/Contracts

Interfaces are the seams between this app and everything outside it. Every external system gets one, so a flow runs
end to end with only the outside faked (`tests/CLAUDE.md`).

- `Contracts/{X}Client.php` is implemented by `Services/{X}Client.php` and bound in a service provider. Consumers
  depend on the interface.
- Keep contracts **workflow-shaped and minimal**: a port, not a generic HTTP wrapper. No speculative methods.
- Read-only unless the workflow needs a write. A method that deletes, pays, sends or executes remotely is a
  deliberate decision: name it for the workflow and document what it may touch.
- A method returning externally authored text documents that the text is **untrusted**.
- A new or changed method changes what the app can do to the outside world. When it changes a surface, update the
  governing `CLAUDE.md` in the SAME commit.
